# Worktree door

Agents work from **worktrees** (isolated branch copies), not the main checkout, for feature work.

**Push door:** new work = open the worktree door. Need access, a path, or a tool? Ask in seat — self-request is granted; the pathway opens. No pre-emptive blocking; hooks nudge waste, they do not gate curiosity.

## Enter (door in)

- [ ] Correct worktree path and branch match the task
- [ ] Session sensor verdict logged (halt = nudge + self-request, not a hard stop)
- [ ] Intent posted to Vellum

## Inside

- Drafts stay local until finished
- Mac is **read-only for git push** — landing on Beast goes via Cascade-Mac / Devin PR

## Exit (door out)

- [ ] Tests/smoke pass where applicable
- [ ] Artefact in a **shared company path** (not worktree-only)
- [ ] Vellum witness + seat-pass if handing off
- [ ] See `finish-waypoint` and `relay-stop` for PASS protocol

No session ends inside the worktree without opening the door — share outward first.
